<title>USA: USDA backdates Dutch meat import ban due mad cow.</title>
<headline>USDA backdates Dutch meat import ban due mad cow.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department Wednesday pushed back the effective date of a new ban on certain Dutch meat imports due to mad cow disease to March 21 from April 10.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, USDA said it was adding Netherlands to the list of countries where bovine spongiform encephalopathy (BSE) or mad cow disease exists because the disease was detected in a cow there on March 21.</p>
<p>It published an interim rule in the Federal Register that prohibited or restricted imports to the U.S. of certain fresh, chilled, and frozen meat, and certain other animal products and byproducts from ruminants that had been in the Netherlands.</p>
</text>
